issue_context.body:
The [Postgres date parts](https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/functions-datetime.html#FUNCTIONS-DATETIME-EXTRACT) are a bit different from ours, so we should fix the discrepancies:
* `offset` should be called `timezone`, `timezone_hour` and `timezone_minute`, with (signed) units of seconds, hours and minutes;
* `century`, `decade` and `millennium` should be checked for extreme values;
* We should add support for `julian` (actually modified/midnight Julian day) and `isoyear`;

review_comments:
Maybe a little too nitpicky:

I really like this control flow pattern, I've never seen it used before though, and I'm afraid it might be a little confusing because we don't use it anywhere else.

Since the code that should be executed for the paths that exit the block is quite small, maybe we can remove it here and just early-return instead

```c++
if (arguments[0]->HasParameter() || !arguments[0]->IsFoldable()) {
	return BindAdapter<data_t>(context, bound_function, arguments, nullptr);
}
```
